===============================================================================

User asked: "create a model that can run on the machine it is able to do swiping
properly but the thing is sometimes there is a problem with the word it detects
you have access to the machine create a python venv and train it for our use
case do you think that will be better?"

Then supplied: FUTO's model description, the swipe.futo.org dataset card, and
the full FUTO Swipe paper (arXiv 2606.25247, "Layout-Agnostic Neural Swipe
Decoding", Miller & Kostarevas, FUTO, June 2026).

ANSWER GIVEN: Yes, clearly better — roughly +13 to +20 points of top-1.
Justification is measured, not assumed:
  - The paper's Table 2 benchmarks SHARK2 at 80.05% top-1 on English QWERTY and
    their encoder at 92.94%.
  - The keyboard's existing geometric decoder IS a SHARK2-family template
    matcher (corridor + shape + location + frequency prior).
  - I measured that existing decoder on the real FUTO test set: 78.66% top-1
    (extended lexicon), within 1.4 points of the paper's independent SHARK2
    implementation. That cross-check validates the whole harness.

