## 4. DATASET
===============================================================================

`futo-org/swipe.futo.org` on HuggingFace, MIT licensed (clean to train on and
ship). Downloaded to `ml/data/hf/` (~6.4 GB):
  train.jsonl 5.16 GB, dev.jsonl 304 MB, test.jsonl 270 MB,
  swipe-2..5 subsets, and swipe-5/layouts/*.json (11 layouts).

Record schema (one swipe per line):
  id, session, timestamp, word, canvas_width, canvas_height, orientation,
  data: [{t: epoch_ms, x: 0..1, y: 0..1}, ...], sentence, word_idx,
  potentially_invalid_sentence, distance

Key points:
- x,y are ALREADY normalized to [0,1] of the keyboard canvas, and the layout
  json uses the same space. Directly compatible.
- `distance` >= ~100000 is a skip sentinel. Filter it.
- `sentence` + `word_idx` give REAL preceding-word context — this is what a
  ContextLM would train on (not yet built, see section 10).
- `session` enables speaker-disjoint splits (the released splits already are).

Packed to `ml/data/packed/{train,dev,test}/` by `ml/swipe/preprocess.py`:
  train 896,274 swipes / 10,719 sessions (paper says 939,550 — I filter ~4.6%
  more via distance + min-length), dev 51,751, test 47,552.
  Files per split: traces.npy (N,64,2 fp16), labels.npy, offsets.npy,
  durations.npy, sessions.npy, words.txt

PREPROCESSING CONVENTION (must match on-device exactly, see section 7):
  resample raw (x,y,t) to 60 Hz, then to T=64 points evenly spaced IN TIME
  (not arc length). Time spacing is what preserves the dwell signal.
  Stores RAW (x,y), not derived features, because augmentation must act on
  coordinates jointly with the layout before features are computed.

