## 5. MODEL ARCHITECTURE (reconstructed from the paper)
===============================================================================

File: `ml/swipe/model.py`. 633,697 params vs paper's stated 635K — the match
confirms the reconstruction. Breakdown: stem 5,248 / blocks 545,440 /
adapter 65,792 / coeff 16,448 / gate 257.

The key reconstruction detail: "expansion 4" means 1x1 to 4*H=512 then GLU
halves it to 256, then project 256->128. (Expanding to 512 *after* GLU would
give ~1.04M params and not match.)

Pipeline:
  raw (B,2,64)
  -> TrajectoryFeatures: Savitzky-Golay 7-tap order-2 -> 8 features
     (x, y, vx, vy, ax, ay, speed, curvature clamped [-2,2])
  -> stem Conv1d(8->128, k=5, pad=2)
  -> 5x TCNBlock, dilations {1,2,3,5,8}, width 128:
       depthwise Conv1d(k=7, dilated) -> BatchNorm -> Linear(128->512)
       -> GLU(->256) -> GRN(256) -> Linear(256->128) -> SqueezeExcite(r=4)
       -> residual
  -> adapter Conv1d(128->256, k=2, stride=2) + BN   [T 64->32]
  -> two heads: coeff Linear(256->64), gate Linear(256->1). BOTH ZERO-INIT.

SPECTRAL SPATIAL HEAD (this is the layout-agnostic trick):
  Phi[k,(u,v)] = cos(pi*u*x_k) * cos(pi*v*y_k), u,v in 0..7  (N_DCT=8, 64 coeff)
  key logits z_t = c_t @ Phi^T
  The network NEVER learns a per-key parameter. The keyboard is sampled from an
  emitted 2D spatial pattern at inference time.

CTC EMISSION FACTORIZATION (blank gate):
  log p[t,k]     = log_softmax(z_t)[k] + log(lambda_t)   for characters
  log p[t,blank] = log(1 - lambda_t)
  where lambda_t = sigmoid(gate_t). Blank index = 26.

LOSS: CTC + 0.05 * emission-count penalty
  L_emit = mean( max(0, L_target - sum_t lambda_t)^2 )   -- one-sided,
  penalizes under-emission only; over-emission left to CTC.
  NOTE: paper is ambiguous (alpha=0.05 inside Eq 7 AND 0.05 weight in Table 10,
  which would double-count to 0.0025). I use a single 0.05, exposed as
  `--emit-weight`.

